Z||000004||theogre||11-09-1999||02:38 AM||||Fiero rerelease...... not in your lifetime.<P>there were some reports of an Opel mid engine car....... Pontiac reportedly wants it if it ever comes to the U.S.. Odds of that are slim.<P>You have to understand a bit of how large U.S. companies work. If you think the U.S. government is politically divided then you've never worked for DuPont or a car maker. these people really do fight over who has the most desktop space, in square inches. It's really quite sad to watch.<P>Every bit of history I can find without a federal law suit indicates that Fiero died an entirely political death. Kind of like the ERA did a few years ago, and the Second Amendment is doing now. Pontiac will likely never be allowed to use the Fiero name again let alone build a mid engine in the U.S. or Canadian plants. To import one is almost as bad and about as unlikely.||||reg||1
